From: mempage4k <mempage4k@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] wgpu-core: wait for the GPU before taking the snatch lock
 in poll

Device::poll took the device's snatch lock for reading, then waited for
the GPU while holding it. A thread waiting for a submission to complete
(a completion thread, frames-in-flight pacing) therefore held the lock for
up to a frame, and every writer (Buffer::destroy, Texture::destroy) waited
that long; the lock is fair, so every other reader queued behind the
writer too: command encoding, resource creation, submits. On a phone
streaming the world this was 7-12 ms of stall a frame on the submit
thread, and recording slowed with it. The wait now happens before the
lock is taken; `maintain` waits again (immediately done) and reports
errors as before.

---
 src/device/resource.rs | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

--- a/src/device/resource.rs
+++ b/src/device/resource.rs
@@ -794,6 +794,25 @@
         &self,
         poll_type: wgt::PollType<crate::SubmissionIndex>,
     ) -> (UserClosures, Result<wgt::PollStatus, WaitIdleError>) {
+        // re5osx: the GPU is waited for before the snatch lock is taken. Held
+        // for reading through the wait, the lock kept every writer (a buffer
+        // or texture destroyed) waiting until the GPU was done, and with them
+        // every other reader queued behind the writer: recording, resource
+        // creation, submits, on all threads. `maintain` waits again (no time
+        // once done) and reports what goes wrong.
+        if let wgt::PollType::Wait {
+            submission_index,
+            timeout,
+        } = poll_type
+        {
+            let last = self
+                .last_successful_submission_index
+                .load(Ordering::Acquire);
+            let target = submission_index.unwrap_or(last);
+            if target <= last {
+                let _ = unsafe { self.raw().wait(self.fence.as_ref(), target, timeout) };
+            }
+        }
         let snatch_guard = self.snatchable_lock.read();
         let maintain_result = self.maintain(poll_type, snatch_guard);
 
